UPDATE public.news_articles SET title='Strengthening Youth Sailor Privacy: Consent-Gated Photos, Private Evidence, and Claim Protections', summary='How public competition records, optional profile sharing, approved profile claims and private workspaces fit together for youth sailors and their families.', body='Because youth sailing records involve minor athletes, SailorPath is built around a strict separation between the public competition record and private athlete or family data. Over the past week, we shipped a series of security and privacy upgrades across public profiles, file storage, and claim workflows.

## Verified Results by Default, Optional Sharing by Choice

Public sailor profiles bring together published competition history—regatta finishes, event sail numbers, class standings and recorded awards. Public records may also include nationality, gender, club and birth year.

• Profile photos and avatars are stored in private buckets and are never publicly served unless an authorised profile owner or verified parent/guardian has explicitly enabled public sharing.
• Full dates of birth and weight are private unless an authorised profile manager chooses to share them. Birth year may appear as part of the public competition record.
• Personal race notes, equipment locker items, and coach debriefs live exclusively inside authenticated Sailor, Parent, and Coach workspaces.

## Hardened Evidence Storage and Claim Quotas

When sailors or parents submit supporting documentation or result evidence, those uploads are now governed by stricter storage policies:

• Supporting evidence files are restricted to accounts with an approved sailor or guardian claim and are served only through short-lived, authorised access checks.
• Per-user upload quotas and file validation checks protect the platform against automated abuse while keeping legitimate result verification fast.

## International Championship Awards on Public Profiles

Official category awards and recorded podium finishes appear together on sailor profiles. Event and source links let visitors check the relevant scorecard or published award evidence. Profiles can include separate girls'' awards, U16/U12 prizes and double-handed helm and crew honours.

Awards now appear newest first. Visitors can change the sort order and combine year, date range, location, boat class, medal and text filters. The medal totals reflect the filtered list.', updated_at='2026-11-03T14:25:00.000+08:00'::timestamptz
WHERE slug='privacy-first-profiles-guardian-consent-and-evidence-protections' AND status='published' AND (title,summary,body) IS DISTINCT FROM ('Strengthening Youth Sailor Privacy: Consent-Gated Photos, Private Evidence, and Claim Protections','How public competition records, optional profile sharing, approved profile claims and private workspaces fit together for youth sailors and their families.','Because youth sailing records involve minor athletes, SailorPath is built around a strict separation between the public competition record and private athlete or family data. Over the past week, we shipped a series of security and privacy upgrades across public profiles, file storage, and claim workflows.

## Verified Results by Default, Optional Sharing by Choice

Public sailor profiles bring together published competition history—regatta finishes, event sail numbers, class standings and recorded awards. Public records may also include nationality, gender, club and birth year.

• Profile photos and avatars are stored in private buckets and are never publicly served unless an authorised profile owner or verified parent/guardian has explicitly enabled public sharing.
• Full dates of birth and weight are private unless an authorised profile manager chooses to share them. Birth year may appear as part of the public competition record.
• Personal race notes, equipment locker items, and coach debriefs live exclusively inside authenticated Sailor, Parent, and Coach workspaces.

## Hardened Evidence Storage and Claim Quotas

When sailors or parents submit supporting documentation or result evidence, those uploads are now governed by stricter storage policies:

• Supporting evidence files are restricted to accounts with an approved sailor or guardian claim and are served only through short-lived, authorised access checks.
• Per-user upload quotas and file validation checks protect the platform against automated abuse while keeping legitimate result verification fast.

## International Championship Awards on Public Profiles

Official category awards and recorded podium finishes appear together on sailor profiles. Event and source links let visitors check the relevant scorecard or published award evidence. Profiles can include separate girls'' awards, U16/U12 prizes and double-handed helm and crew honours.

Awards now appear newest first. Visitors can change the sort order and combine year, date range, location, boat class, medal and text filters. The medal totals reflect the filtered list.') RETURNING slug;

